# Terminal Dialogs

`dialog` provides small, modal terminal dialogs for application
using the Termina vocabulary. It is intended for information,
acknowledgement, and single-line input rather than menus or
full-screen editing.

DEPENDENCIES:

- termina
- rng

Before displaying a dialog, configure the terminal dimensions
with `dialog:configure` (rows followed by columns). The caller
is responsible for selecting an appropriate terminal input mode
and redrawing any application UI after a dialog is dismissed.

`dialog:show`, `dialog:error`, and `dialog:help` take a message
followed by a title. `dialog:read`, `dialog:password`, and
`dialog:prompt` take a prompt followed by a title and return the
entered line.

~~~
#0 'dialog:Width  var-n
#0 'dialog:Height var-n
#0 'dialog:Row    var-n
#0 'dialog:Col    var-n

#52 'DIALOG:WIDTH const

:dialog:configure (:nn-)
  !dialog:Width !dialog:Height ;

:dialog:setup (:-)
  @dialog:Height #2 &n:div call #2 n:sub !dialog:Row
  @dialog:Width DIALOG:WIDTH n:sub #2 &n:div call !dialog:Col ;

:dialog:bar (:-)
  $+ c:put DIALOG:WIDTH #2 n:sub [ $- c:put ] times $+ c:put ;

:dialog:line (:n-)
  @dialog:Row n:add @dialog:Col vt:row,col
  $| c:put DIALOG:WIDTH #2 n:sub [ sp ] times $| c:put ;

:dialog:draw (:-)
  dialog:setup
  fg:cyan @dialog:Row @dialog:Col vt:row,col dialog:bar
  #1 dialog:line #2 dialog:line #3 dialog:line
  @dialog:Row #4 n:add @dialog:Col vt:row,col dialog:bar
  vt:reset ;

:dialog:title (:s-)
  fg:red @dialog:Row #1 n:add @dialog:Col #2 n:add vt:row,col s:put ;

:dialog:text (:s-)
  fg:yellow @dialog:Row #2 n:add @dialog:Col #2 n:add vt:row,col
  DIALOG:WIDTH #4 n:sub s:left s:put ;

:dialog:show (:ss-)
  dialog:draw dialog:title dialog:text
  fg:cyan @dialog:Row #3 n:add @dialog:Col #2 n:add vt:row,col
  'Press_any_key s:put vt:reset c:get drop ;

:dialog:error (:ss-) dialog:show ;
:dialog:help  (:ss-) dialog:show ;
~~~

# Single-Line Input

`dialog:read` displays a normal, visible input line.
`dialog:password` returns the same input string, but displays
one or two randomly selected asterisks for each entered
character. Both readers accept CR or LF as the end of input, and
support backspace and delete.

~~~
#0 'dialog:Password var-n
#0 'dialog:MaskCount var-n
'dialog:MaskWidths d:create #512 allot

:dialog:done? (c-f)
  [ ASCII:CR eq? ] [ ASCII:LF eq? ] bi or ;

:dialog:backspace? (c-cf)
  dup [ ASCII:BS eq? ] [ ASCII:DEL eq? ] bi or ;

:dialog:erase-width (n-)
  [ #1 vt:left sp #1 vt:left ] times ;

:dialog:erase (:-)
  buffer:size #2 gteq?
  [ @dialog:Password
    [ &dialog:MaskCount v:dec
      &dialog:MaskWidths @dialog:MaskCount a:fetch dialog:erase-width ]
    [ #1 dialog:erase-width ] choose ] if ;

:dialog:mask (:-)
  n:random #2 n:mod #1 n:add dup
  &dialog:MaskWidths @dialog:MaskCount a:store
  &dialog:MaskCount v:inc
  [ $* c:put ] times ;

:dialog:echo (c-)
  dup dialog:backspace? [ drop dialog:erase ]
  [ dup dialog:done? [ drop ]
    [ @dialog:Password [ drop dialog:mask ] [ c:put ] choose ] choose ] choose ;

:dialog:check-bs (c-c)
  dup dialog:backspace? [ buffer:size #2 gteq?
    [ buffer:get drop ] if buffer:get drop ] if ;

:dialog:input (:ss-s)
  dialog:draw dialog:title dialog:text
  [ #0 !dialog:MaskCount s:empty buffer:set
    [ c:get dup buffer:add dup dialog:echo dialog:check-bs dialog:done? ] until
    buffer:start s:chop ] buffer:preserve
  vt:reset ;

:dialog:read (:ss-s)
  #0 !dialog:Password dialog:input ;

:dialog:password (:ss-s)
  #-1 !dialog:Password dialog:input ;

:dialog:prompt (:ss-s) dialog:read ;
~~~
